# SetWorkspace.srv — move/resize the planner's collision workspace (the Mapper
# TSDF/ESDF grid extent).
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES
#   `extent`/`center` are the launch file's `mapper_extent_xyz` /
#   `mapper_grid_center`. Setting them:
#     * updates the two ROS parameters (so a later read sees what is in force),
#     * rebuilds the Mapper to the new grid (dropping the TSDF/ESDF currently
#       integrated — the old voxels no longer cover the requested box),
#     * resizes the solvers' voxel collision cache to match, which rebuilds
#       every solver (~20 s, the same build-time property as
#       set_collision_cache),
#     * republishes the wireframe on <node>/mapper_workspace so the drawn box
#       and the collision world move together.
#
#   An empty list for either field means "leave that one unchanged", so one call
#   can move the centre and keep the size (or vice versa). The response always
#   echoes the values actually in force afterwards, so a caller never has to
#   remember what it sent.
#
# GUARDS
#   Refused while an execution goal is active (a ~20 s blocking rebuild is not
#   safe against an in-progress trajectory) — same guard as set_collision_cache
#   and set_joint_locks. When perception is inactive (use_mapper=False, or no
#   camera/laser configured) the values and the marker still move, but there is
#   no Mapper to rebuild; `perception_active` reports which case applied.

# --- Request ---
# New box centre, [x, y, z] in the base frame. Empty => unchanged.
float64[] center

# New box size, [x, y, z] in the base frame, metres (all > 0).
# Empty => unchanged.
float64[] extent

---

# --- Response ---
bool success
string message

# Values in force after the call (never the request verbatim — the server's
# answer is the truth a UI should display).
string frame_id
float64[] center
float64[] extent
float64 voxel_size

# See GetWorkspace.srv: whether a Mapper exists to have been rebuilt.
bool perception_active
